{
	UniqueName: "TutorialMove",
	Catalyst: "NONE",
	QuestName: "Quest.CampaignPrologue",
	PartyMakeupReq: "ANY",
	FireImmediately: "true",
	AutoAdvanceTime: "4",
	MetaData: "tutorialMove",
	Priority: "100",
	ClearQueueOnFinish: "true",
	ToolTip: ["Move|Sprint|Swap|Drawing Paths|Undo Movement", "On their turn, each character can 'Move' as many hexes as their Movement stat allows. By moving onto a green hex, they can still perform an action afterward.|To cover more ground, they can 'Sprint' onto the dashed grey hexes, but doing so will end their turn.|You can 'Swap' places with an ally by moving onto their location. Swapping is useful for setting up attacks, or for getting an ally out of harm's way.|By holding <sprite name=\"PC-shift\">, you can draw a custom movement route.^By holding <sprite name=\"XboxOne-rt\">, you can draw a custom movement route.|To undo a movement, click the undo button on the hotbar, or press the hotkey assigned to it (<sprite name=\"PC-e\">). If you take damage or trigger a stage hazard you will be unable to undo your movement.\n\nLet's move the Stormcaller into cover by clicking 'LMB' <sprite name=\"PC-leftClick\"> on the indicated hex.^To undo a movement, click the undo button on the hotbar. If you take damage or trigger a stage hazard you will be unable to undo your movement.\n\nLet's move the Stormcaller into cover by pressing <sprite name=\"XboxOne-a\"> on the indicated hex."],
	Text: [""],
}
