{
	UniqueName: "TutorialLineOfSight",
	Catalyst: "NONE",
	QuestName: "Quest.CampaignPrologue",
	PartyMakeupReq: "ANY",
	FireImmediately: "true",
	AutoAdvanceTime: "4",
	MetaData: "tutorialLineOfSight",
	Priority: "100",
	ClearQueueOnFinish: "true",
	ToolTip: ["Line of Sight|No Line of Sight|Partial Line of Sight|Attacking from Cover|Channeled Abilities", "Most attacks and abilities are subject to Line of Sight. When targeting, a red eye indicates that there is no line of sight, while a yellow eye indicates a partial line of sight.|Large obstacles such as pillars can block line of sight entirely. When a character has no vision of an enemy, they are unable to directly target them. |Smaller obstacles, such as a barrel, crate, or character will partially obscure line of sight under the right circumstances. A target who is partially visible will receive 50% less damage from attacks.|By taking cover directly behind a small obstacle, you can look over the obstacle and gain full vision of an enemy, while remaining only partially visible in return.|The Stormcaller's 'Conduit' ability can devastate a single enemy from range, but takes a few turns to channel. You can see where a channel will finish by looking at the blue indicator arrow on the turn order.\n\nSelect the 'Conduit' ability and target the enemy archer."],
	Text: [""],
}
{
	UniqueName: "TutorialAwareness",
	Catalyst: "NONE",
	QuestName: "Quest.CampaignPrologue",
	PartyMakeupReq: "ANY",
	FireImmediately: "true",
	AutoAdvanceTime: "4",
	MetaData: "tutorialawareness",
	Priority: "100",
	ClearQueueOnFinish: "true",
	ToolTip: ["Avoiding Attacks of Opportunity", "With the nearest enemy Stunned, the Pyrolancer can safely move past their zone of control without incurring an Attack of Opportunity. Attacks of Opportunity can also be avoided by using abilities that incorporate movement, or by utilizing the 'Swap' action.\n\nLet's aid the Guardian and Sprint to engage her target."],
	Text: [""],
}
